{"availability":"available","full":"rejifald/StitchAPI","name":"StitchAPI","description":"The agent-native runtime where a typed, declarative stitch replaces fetch — for humans and agents alike.","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":20,"forks":0,"created":"2024-08-16T14:30:57Z","updated":"2026-10-05T16:09:39Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://stitchapi.dev","topics":["api","mcp","mcp-server","npm-package","typescript"],"demo":"https://stitchapi.dev/?utm_source=github#playground","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T00:25:38.110Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T00:25:38.110Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T00:25:38.110Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T00:25:38.110Z","stars":20,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["API stitching: turn any API into a typed, resilient function. Declare an endpoint once — its types, auth, and resilience — and call it like a local function. No server, no codegen, no config files. The same definition answers to your code, the CLI, and an AI agent alike.","📚 stitchapi.dev — documentation, guides & live playground","Zero runtime dependencies · 21 kB min+gzip — a typical import { stitch } tree-shakes to 19 kB, and with no transitive tree there is nothing else to install or audit. The cache engine and the OTLP exporter load lazily, on first use, so they are not in those figures. The size is an enforced budget in CI, not an aspiration."],"features":["Atomic, not spec-first. Spec-based generators (openapi-generator, Orval, Kubb, …) need a complete OpenAPI document first — and most real-world APIs (internal, undocumented, the long tail) never get one. A stitch needs a…","A runtime, not a code generator. No generated SDK to commit, diff, and regenerate. The declaration is the client, validated on every live call — so a silently renamed field is a loud, leveled drift signal, not an…","Resilience is declared, not hand-rolled. Retries, throttling, timeouts, circuit breaking, pagination — configuration on the stitch, uniform across every integration.","Auth is a boundary. A stitch owns its credential and lifecycle; callers get a capability, not the credential. That matters double when the caller is an AI agent.","Agents are first-class callers. One definition is a function, a CLI command, an HTTP endpoint, and an MCP tool — returning structured, schema-validated, traceable results instead of opaque bytes."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/rejifald/StitchAPI/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"d4d3028dd717766c8cb63c3f1276b2aca96d00c1c97d495194cec0c4c27d6f3e","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T00:25:38.169Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T00:25:38.169Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"API stitching: turn any API into a typed, resilient function. Declare an endpoint once — its types, auth, and resilience — and call it like a local function. No server, no codegen, no config files. The same definition answers to your code, the CLI, and an AI agent alike.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/rejifald/StitchAPI/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"api_key","status":"required","text":"Auth as a boundary — bearer, apiKey, basic, cookieSession (auto-login/re-login), oauth2; secrets resolve at call time and never reach the caller.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/rejifald/StitchAPI/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Auth as a boundary — bearer, apiKey, basic, cookieSession (auto-login/re-login), oauth2; secrets resolve at call time and never reach the caller.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/rejifald/StitchAPI/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"api_key","status":"required","text":"bearer, apiKey, and basic are header strategies; oauth2() runs the client-credentials grant and caches/refreshes the token; and cookieSession runs a login, captures the cookie, replays it, and re-logs-in when the wall returns — the caller never sees the password or writes the cookie dance.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/rejifald/StitchAPI/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"bearer, apiKey, and basic are header strategies; oauth2() runs the client-credentials grant and caches/refreshes the token; and cookieSession runs a login, captures the cookie, replays it, and re-logs-in when the wall returns — the caller never sees the password or writes the cookie dance.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/rejifald/StitchAPI/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"d4d3028dd717766c8cb63c3f1276b2aca96d00c1c97d495194cec0c4c27d6f3e","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/rejifald/StitchAPI/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T00:25:38.170Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-05T16:09:39Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/rejifald/StitchAPI/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T00:25:38.172Z","hash":"d4d3028dd717766c8cb63c3f1276b2aca96d00c1c97d495194cec0c4c27d6f3e","originalBytes":34492,"storedBytes":34492,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["stitch","stitchapi","auth","drift","call","one","every","const","import","cache","schema","throttle","typed","validated","data","endpoint","stream","path","request","response","runtime","fetch","full","output","run","seam","what","api","event","timeout","trace","default","error","getuser","http","never","per","retry","same","sse","store","surfaces","validation","agent","any","await","config","field","get","resilience","budget","code","core","docs","documentation","function","guide","live","mcp","packages","pick","retries","user","caching","cli","declared","each","env","listusers","observability","once","only","own","params","server","tool","url","when","zod","attempts","bearer","body","cache-fingerprint","caller","circuit","command","contract","credential","declare","errors","graphql","host","install","level","leveled","library","local","nothing","openapi","raw","required","returns","sink","stitches","strategy","them","total","workflo